# 05 — AI subsystem rules (governance, approval, memory, output)

**Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root FIRST**, then this file. Loading order
(AGENTS.md §1): `AGENTS.md` → `memory/AI_MEMORY.md` + `memory/SECURITY_MEMORY.md`
→ `context/*.md` → `rules/global/*` + `rules/security/*` + `rules/ai/*` →
`skills/ai/*` → `docs/AI.md` + `docs/ai/*` → code + tests → **then** edit. Never
edit first and understand later.

The single source of truth for governance/policy is `memory/AI_MEMORY.md` and
`docs/AI.md`. The shared, dependency-free contracts live in `packages/ai`
(`safety.ts`, `redaction.ts`, `model-router.ts`, `evaluators.ts`, `prompts.ts`,
`types.ts`). The live subsystem is `apps/api/src/modules/ai` (`chat/`, `memory/`,
`orchestrator/`, `prompt-registry/`, `usage-budget/`, `writeback/`, `eval/`,
`semantic-search/`, `feature-catalog/`, `simulation/`). The full enforced backend
rule list (rules #88–100 cover AI) is `apps/api/CLAUDE.md`; AI-UI rules
(#41–63) are in `apps/web/CLAUDE.md`. When in doubt, those files win.

Tooling: **pnpm only, Node 22.** Blocking typecheck is `pnpm typecheck` (`tsc`);
`pnpm typecheck:fast` (`tsgo`) is advisory only. **Never work on `main`** —
branch first.

## 1. Governance — analyze/suggest, never silently act

- AI may **analyze and suggest**. AI **must NOT silently execute** destructive
  security/infra actions (run a playbook, isolate a host, mutate a case/alert).
  Those are `approval-required` (AGENTS.md §7; api CLAUDE.md #97).
- Classify every AI-proposed action with `AiActionCategory` from
  `@auraspear/ai` (`safety.ts`): `ANALYSIS_ONLY` / `SUGGESTED` /
  `APPROVAL_REQUIRED` / `AUTO_ALLOWED`. Never invent ad-hoc category strings —
  use the enum (web CLAUDE.md #44, #50–52).
- Decide approval via `evaluateApproval(action)` — it is conservative by design:
  anything `destructive` or HIGH/CRITICAL risk requires approval; `AUTO_ALLOWED`
  bypasses approval only for non-destructive low/medium risk and must be
  allow-listed per tenant.

## 2. Approval gating (persisted, before execution)

- **No approval-required action runs without a persisted `ApprovalRequest`
  record created BEFORE execution** (api CLAUDE.md #97). Never execute on the
  optimistic path; never auto-approve in any environment.
- The action also needs the caller's RBAC permission — every AI endpoint carries
  `@RequirePermission(Permission.MODULE_ACTION)` (api CLAUDE.md #25). No auth
  bypass, no `NODE_ENV`-gated shortcuts (api CLAUDE.md #23, #56).
- Agent configs are constrained: validate against `AiAgentId` /
  `AiProviderMode` enums; `trigger_config` JSON is validated by a mode-specific
  Zod schema (no arbitrary JSON); every trigger evaluation is logged with
  trigger type, result, `agent_id`, `tenant_id` (api CLAUDE.md #92–94, #99).

## 3. Provider routing (cascade, never short-circuit)

- Routing is a cascade: **`bedrock → llm_apis → openclaw_gateway → rule-based`**.
  Try **ALL** configured connectors before falling back; never short-circuit to
  rule-based after a single provider failure (api CLAUDE.md #88;
  web CLAUDE.md #30).
- **No mock/placeholder providers in production code** — no `BEDROCK_MOCK` or
  any env-gated mock mode. Call the real SDK/API; on failure, try the next
  connector (api CLAUDE.md #89). Rule-based output is allowed only when no
  connector is configured and must be labeled `model: 'rule-based'`.
- Record the provider/model actually used in the audit log and in result
  provenance.

## 4. Tenant isolation & connector secrets

- AI memory, transcripts, findings, agent configs, and usage budgets are
  **tenant-scoped**. Every backend AI query/`update`/`delete` is scoped by
  `tenantId` (`where: { id, tenantId }` — never by `id` alone; api CLAUDE.md #26).
- AI investigation **validates resource tenant ownership** (alert/case belongs to
  the caller's tenant) before acting — no cross-tenant investigation
  (api CLAUDE.md #48).
- Connector credentials and OSINT source API keys are **AES-256-GCM encrypted at
  rest** (`encryption.utility.ts`); custom OSINT source URLs pass **SSRF
  validation** (`SsrfUtility.validateUrl()`) at input time, before encrypting
  (api CLAUDE.md #95, #96). Never put OSINT keys in frontend state/`localStorage`.

## 5. Redaction & memory (no secrets near the model)

- **Redact PII/secrets BEFORE** sending context to a model and BEFORE persisting
  transcripts: `redact()` from `@auraspear/ai` (`redaction.ts`) — covers private
  keys, JWTs, AWS keys, bearer tokens, generic `secret=`/`password=`, email,
  IPv4. Use the `keep` argument only when an indicator (e.g. an IP) is the very
  thing under investigation.
- **AI memory (`UserMemory`) must never store secrets**; it is tenant-scoped.
  Memory retrieval is **non-blocking** — a retrieval/embedding failure never
  crashes chat (web CLAUDE.md AI Memory section).
- Never store AI transcripts in `localStorage` — server-side session only
  (web CLAUDE.md #46). Credentials/tokens are redacted from logs and audit
  interceptors.

## 6. Output safety (never raw HTML)

- **Never render raw AI output as HTML.** Render markdown via a safe renderer or
  plain text. `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with AI content is banned
  (`react/no-danger: error`; web CLAUDE.md #43). Transform inter-agent JSON to
  human-readable before rendering (web CLAUDE.md #58).
- Every AI output is **attributable**: provenance (provider, model, confidence,
  prompt version, token usage) + citations where applicable. Each AI surface
  shows loading / error / confidence / provider attribution + a regenerate and a
  dismiss affordance (web CLAUDE.md #42, #47).
- Structured blocks (risk gauges, IOC tables, MITRE maps, timelines) use the
  standardized `apps/web/src/components/ai-renderer/` components — no ad-hoc
  inline rendering (web CLAUDE.md #53). Every AI surface registers in the
  `AiFeatureKey` catalog before implementation (web CLAUDE.md #49).

## 7. Budget & evaluation

- **Check the per-agent token quota before calling the provider**
  (api CLAUDE.md #98); usage lives in `apps/api/src/modules/ai/usage-budget/`.
- AI endpoints are rate-limited: `@Throttle({ default: { limit: 10, ttl: 60000 } })`
  at controller level (api CLAUDE.md #33).
- Behavior changes go through the golden-case harness in `@auraspear/ai`
  (`evaluators.ts`) / `apps/api/src/modules/ai/eval/`. **Safety assertions fail a
  run regardless of pass rate** — do not relax them to make eval pass.

## 8. Code-quality invariants (apply here too)

- **No `any`. No `eslint-disable` / `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error`.** Fix the
  root cause (both apps, rule #1–2). No `!`, no `==`/`!=`, no `var`, no
  `console.log`.
- Declarations have a home file: enums in `<module>.enums.ts` (backend) /
  `src/enums/` (frontend); types in `<module>.types.ts` / `src/types/`; constants
  in `<module>.constants.ts` / `src/lib/constants/`. **String literal unions are
  banned** — use enums (`AiActionCategory`, `AiProviderMode`, `AiTriggerMode`,
  `AiAgentId`). Backend OSINT/builtin source definitions live in constants files,
  never hardcoded in services (api CLAUDE.md #100).
- `packages/ai` stays **dependency-free** (no SDKs, no infra) — provider-agnostic
  contracts + pure utilities only (see its `index.ts` header).

## 9. Branch & validate before claiming green

- Branch first (`feat/...`, `fix/...`, `chore/...`); never destructive commands
  unless required + documented. **Prove before removing** any AI file/dep/env/
  proxy/i18n key (`rules/global/branch-safety.md`).
- Before claiming done, run `pnpm typecheck` (+ `pnpm lint`, `pnpm build`, AI
  eval). **Never say "all green" unless the required gates actually passed.** End
  with the AGENTS.md §13 report block. The `qa-gatekeeper` subagent rejects
  claims without command output.

